    "https://www.paulsmiths.edu/careers/?jobId=0a4541b8-b4ed-73d4-9b2c-42a63a8be27d": {
      "title": "Careers - Paul Smith's College",
      "description": "Careers - Paul Smith's College Skip Main Navigation Paul Smith's College Home For You For You Audience Future Students Current Students Parents & Families Veterans Local Communities Alumni Center & Institutes Center & Institutes Centers Center for Research, Partnerships, and Innovation Adirondack Watershed Institute Institute of Adventure Hospitality & Food Institute of Forestry John Dillon Park Visitor Interpretive Center Menu You are here: Home / Jobs at Paul Smith's College Jobs at Paul Smith's College Jobs at Paul Smith's College At Paul Smith’s College, we believe in investing in our employees’ well-being. We offer a comprehensive benefits package that includes not only robust health, dental, and vision insurance, but generous paid time off, including vacation, personal leave, sick leave, and holidays. We prioritize employee wellness through access to a supportive employee assistance program. A myriad of voluntary benefits are available, including short- & long-term disability insurance, accident insurance, critical illness insurance, and legal assistance. We understand the importance of work-life balance and encourage employees to take advantage of our flexible work options when possible. The College offers eligible employees with a 403(b) retirement plan account and contributes 5% of their salary towards the plan. Employees receive complimentary access to our library, gym, athletic facilities, fitness center, recreational equipment, on-campus sporting events, cultural events, and social activities. Discounts are available for on-campus dining and the college’s Mercantile bookstore. We value our employees’ academic and personal interests and offer tuition remission for employees and their dependents. Employees receive complimentary access to the Paul Smith’s College Visitor Interpretive Center (the VIC), which offers 25 miles of scenic hiking, snowshoeing, and cross-country ski trails, wildlife viewing opportunities, educational programs, and interactive butterfly exhibit. For more information or questions about careers at Paul Smith’s College, please call us at: 518-327-6179 Back to Job Openings Winter Ski Trail Groomer Apply Share Link copied Position : Winter Ski Trail Groomer Status: Temporary/ Seasonal, Non-exempt, ON CALL Department: Visitor’s Interpretive Center (VIC) Reports to: Trails and Facilities Manager Salary: $22.00/hour Description: The Winter Trail Groomer position maintains and grooms 25 miles of trails for various winter activities, including recreational and competitive skiing and snowshoeing. The primary duties are operating and maintaining grooming equipment (snowmobiles, snow cats, etc.). Work hours will include weekends and night shifts. Flexibility in scheduling is essential, as work hours will vary depending on weather conditions and event needs. Duties & Responsibilities: Prepare groomed trail surfaces for a variety of configurations and uses including recreational and competitive events for skate, classic cross-country skiing and snowshoeing. Operate grooming equipment safely and efficiently including tracked ATV’s and UTV’s, snowmobiles, drag and roller equipment, and a snow cat (Piston Bully 100) with dual track setters and a 12-way blade. Perform routine, daily maintenance checks on equipment prior to utilization. Conduct necessary repairs to equipment as needed to ensure safe and reliable equipment, and a well-maintained trail system. Operate power saw and hand tools to improve trails including the use of chainsaws, pole saws, and snow shovels. Collaborate with college staff and others to plan and implement winter trail races and events Implement daily, seasonal, short and long-term maintenance plans in coordination with supervisor for equipment, tools, snow cat barn, and trail infrastructure. Coordinate with supervisor for budgeting and purchasing tools, equipment, fluids, and maintenance items for equipment. Daily inspection of trail system mitigating safety and comfort concerns including trail surface and tree management. Assessment and repair including shoveling trailside benches and stocking trailside outhouses. Installation and monitoring of trail wayfinding signage and race signage as needed. Manage the on-site needs of the grooming operation including general upkeep of workspace, fuel and fluids, signage, and providing a published daily grooming report. Qualifications: Demonstrated experience in operating heavy equipment. Demonstrated knowledge of Nordic skiing, its various disciplines, and the varieties of groomed terrain that support it. Desire and ability to operate power saw and hand tools to improve trails including the use of chainsaws, pole saws, and snow shovels. Knowledge of and desire to maintain safety at the workplace regarding power tools, heavy equipment, and risk in the outdoor winter environment. Ability to work weekends, holidays, irregular hours, and evening work a must. Ability to work with a broad range of diverse individuals and groups to form a safe and inclusive workplace. Preferred: 2-years’ experience operating and maintaining Nordic ski grooming equipment including a Piston Bully 100, snowmobiles, ATV, and UTV’s. Proficiency in preparation of groomed trail surfaces for a variety of configurations and uses including recreational and competitive events for skate, classic cross-country skiing and snowshoeing. Demonstrated knowledge of event preparation including placement of appropriate signage, V-Boards, flagging and grooming to produce desired race configurations. Preferably certified in, or willing to obtain the following certifications: Wilderness First Responder, CPR and First Aid, valid driver’s license, chainsaw safety certifications, heavy equipment operator certifications. Physical Requirements: Environmental Conditions? The Work of this position is primarily performed outdoors. Seasonal temperatures should be expected and various noise levels dependent on equipment being used to perform job duties should be expected. Lifting and Carrying Occasionally lifting and carrying of equipment weighing 50 lbs. Equipment and related debris are of various shapes and sizes so may require unusual gripping points. Mobility Occasional standing and walking across snow covered surfaces potentially utilizing snowshoes. Ability to bend, stoop, and kneel to pick up items, as necessary. May have to climb some moderately challenging steep hills and hike up to two miles. Frequent need to reach overhead or below waist level to perform work duties. Dexterity and Hand-Eye Coordination Manual dexterity for handling tools and equipment used in the performance of duties. Sensory Requirements Good vision, including color vision, with corrective lenses as necessary. ?? Good hearing with assistive devices as necessary. ?? Paul Smith’s College is an equal opportunity employer. Position descriptions are created that focus on essential functions, using inclusive language, and avoid unnecessary or discriminatory requirements. Review of candidates starts immediately! Apply Paul Smith's College Home 7777 NY-30, Paul Smiths, NY 12970 admissions@paulsmiths.edu Phone 888-873-6570 58° F Mainly clear, partly cloudy, and overcast Social Facebook Instagram X YouTube TikTok Live Webcams Action Visit Apply Request Info Give Bobnet Login Footer About Paul Smith's College Faculty & Staff Directory Graduate Studies Careers Mercantile Library Directions to Paul Smith's College Privacy Policy Request Info News © 2026 Paul Smith's College . All rights reserved Site Menu Search Submit site The Smitty Story Apply for Admission First-Year Applicants Homeschooled Applicants Transfer Applicants International Applicants Graduate Applicants Cost & Aid Tuition & Fees Net Price Calculator Types of Aid Applying for Aid Payment Academics Find a Program Hands-on Learning Academic Support Meet Our Faculty Graduate Studies M.S. Natural Resources Conservation M.P.S. Sustainable Tourism Management Graduate Certificates Battlefish Academy TopGuide Troops to Timber Life at Paul Smith’s College Housing & Dining Local Communities Clubs & Activities Health & Safety Alumni Athletics Search Submit Actions Visit Apply Request Info Give Bobnet Login For You Future Students Current Students Parents & Families Veterans Local Communities Alumni Center & Institutes Center for Research, Partnerships, and Innovation Adirondack Watershed Institute Institute of Adventure Hospitality & Food Institute of Forestry John Dillon Park Visitor Interpretive Center Close Close"
    },
    "https://www.paulsmiths.edu/careers/?jobId=457fcc67-6376-aa18-1b3c-caaa907bde8b": {
      "title": "Careers - Paul Smith's College",
      "description": "Careers - Paul Smith's College Skip Main Navigation Paul Smith's College Home For You For You Audience Future Students Current Students Parents & Families Veterans Local Communities Alumni Center & Institutes Center & Institutes Centers Center for Research, Partnerships, and Innovation Adirondack Watershed Institute Institute of Adventure Hospitality & Food Institute of Forestry John Dillon Park Visitor Interpretive Center Menu You are here: Home / Jobs at Paul Smith's College Jobs at Paul Smith's College Jobs at Paul Smith's College At Paul Smith’s College, we believe in investing in our employees’ well-being. We offer a comprehensive benefits package that includes not only robust health, dental, and vision insurance, but generous paid time off, including vacation, personal leave, sick leave, and holidays. We prioritize employee wellness through access to a supportive employee assistance program. A myriad of voluntary benefits are available, including short- & long-term disability insurance, accident insurance, critical illness insurance, and legal assistance. We understand the importance of work-life balance and encourage employees to take advantage of our flexible work options when possible. The College offers eligible employees with a 403(b) retirement plan account and contributes 5% of their salary towards the plan. Employees receive complimentary access to our library, gym, athletic facilities, fitness center, recreational equipment, on-campus sporting events, cultural events, and social activities. Discounts are available for on-campus dining and the college’s Mercantile bookstore. We value our employees’ academic and personal interests and offer tuition remission for employees and their dependents. Employees receive complimentary access to the Paul Smith’s College Visitor Interpretive Center (the VIC), which offers 25 miles of scenic hiking, snowshoeing, and cross-country ski trails, wildlife viewing opportunities, educational programs, and interactive butterfly exhibit. For more information or questions about careers at Paul Smith’s College, please call us at: 518-327-6179 Back to Job Openings Laboratory Administrative Assistant Apply Share Link copied Position: Laboratory Administrative Assistant Status: Regular, Full-time, Non-Exempt Department: AWI Laboratory Reports to: Laboratory Director Salary: $23.00/hour Description: The Adirondack Watershed Institute is a program of Paul Smith’s College, a private undergraduate college located in the heart of the Adirondack Park in upstate New York. The mission of AWI is to protect clean water, conserve habitat, and support the health and well-being of people in the Adirondacks through scientific inquiry, stewardship, and real-world experiences for students. AWI’s Environmental Research Laboratory holds certification under NYSDOH Environmental Laboratory Accreditation Program (ELAP). The Laboratory Administrative Assistant is a critical low-level position within AWI. This position supports daily laboratory operations by working with laboratory management on administrative duties and serves as the Sample Coordinator responsible for ensuring all samples that arrive at the lab are received and processed correctly, completely, and in a timely manner. This position also serves as the Laboratory Safety Officer. Duties & Responsibilities: Act as the Sample Coordinator responsible for managing the receipt of samples, chain of custody forms, and initial sample processing and preservation. Ensure sample information is entered into the Laboratory Information Management System (LIMS). Assist the lab management with writing and executing lab service agreements and contracts specific to lab work. Coordinate with clients for arranging sampling supplies and sample deliveries. Support efficient laboratory workflow, including scheduling of laboratory operations tasks and analysis. Work with management to coordinate tasks and prioritize sample processing. Oversee purchasing, receiving, and tracking of materials and supplies necessary to operate the lab and meet NYSDOH ELAP traceability requirements. Assist laboratory management in overseeing and maintaining the Environmental Research Laboratory Quality Assurance Management System to NYS DOH ELAP standards. Serve as the Laboratory Safety Officer. Responsible for developing the laboratory safety and chemical hygiene program and ensuring the lab is maintained as a safe working environment. Assist with equipment and instrument maintenance and calibrations. Assist in the hiring, training, and day-to-day supervision of Seasonal Laboratory Technicians and student employees. Contribute to the development of the training program for Seasonal Laboratory Technicians. Update laboratory standard operating procedures as needed. Assist in developing new processes and procedures. Conduct laboratory analysis, as trained. Prepare data for final review. Guarantee analysis and reporting is completed in a timely manner. Support annual quality assurance audits, oversight of staff demonstration of capability, oversight of lab proficiency testing, and the laboratory corrective action system. Contribute data for dissemination through annual reports, research publications, and presentations. Contribute expertise to new project development. Other related duties as assigned. Qualifications: Bachelor of Science degree in Limnology, Aquatic Ecology, Environmental Sciences, or a related field. Two years of working experience and an associate degree, or equivalent college credits, may be substituted for a bachelor’s degree. One year of work experience in an environmental laboratory setting. Understanding of proper sample handling and preservation requirement. Understanding of laboratory QA/QC practices, laboratory instrumentation, and method development. Strong communication skills. Proven ability to multitask. Excellent problem-solving skills. Ability to work in a fast paced, multi-tasking, collaborative environment. Ability to work independently. Preferred: Familiarity with the geography of the Adirondack region. Driver’s license and driving record acceptable to the College’s insurance carrier. Paul Smith’s College is an equal opportunity employer. Position descriptions are created that focus on essential functions, using inclusive language, and avoid unnecessary or discriminatory requirements. Apply Paul Smith's College Home 7777 NY-30, Paul Smiths, NY 12970 admissions@paulsmiths.edu Phone 888-873-6570 64° F Clear sky Social Facebook Instagram X YouTube TikTok Live Webcams Action Visit Apply Request Info Give Bobnet Login Footer About Paul Smith's College Faculty & Staff Directory Graduate Studies Careers Mercantile Library Directions to Paul Smith's College Privacy Policy Request Info News © 2026 Paul Smith's College . All rights reserved Site Menu Search Submit site The Smitty Story Apply for Admission First-Year Applicants Homeschooled Applicants Transfer Applicants International Applicants Graduate Applicants Cost & Aid Tuition & Fees Net Price Calculator Types of Aid Applying for Aid Payment Academics Find a Program Hands-on Learning Work Experience Program Academic Support Meet Our Faculty Graduate Studies M.S. Natural Resources Conservation M.P.S. Sustainable Tourism Management Graduate Certificates Battlefish Academy TopGuide Troops to Timber Life at Paul Smith’s College Housing & Dining Local Communities Clubs & Activities Health & Safety Alumni Athletics Search Submit Actions Visit Apply Request Info Give Bobnet Login For You Future Students Current Students Parents & Families Veterans Local Communities Alumni Center & Institutes Center for Research, Partnerships, and Innovation Adirondack Watershed Institute Institute of Adventure Hospitality & Food Institute of Forestry John Dillon Park Visitor Interpretive Center Close Close"
    },
    "https://www.paulsmiths.edu/careers/?jobId=6267ed42-6737-9243-a6f9-56673e43c0e5": {
      "title": "Careers - Paul Smith's College",
      "description": "Careers - Paul Smith's College Skip Main Navigation Paul Smith's College Home For You For You Audience Future Students Current Students Parents & Families Veterans Local Communities Alumni Center & Institutes Center & Institutes Centers Center for Research, Partnerships, and Innovation Adirondack Watershed Institute Institute of Adventure Hospitality & Food Institute of Forestry John Dillon Park Visitor Interpretive Center Menu You are here: Home / Jobs at Paul Smith's College Jobs at Paul Smith's College Jobs at Paul Smith's College At Paul Smith’s College, we believe in investing in our employees’ well-being. We offer a comprehensive benefits package that includes not only robust health, dental, and vision insurance, but generous paid time off, including vacation, personal leave, sick leave, and holidays. We prioritize employee wellness through access to a supportive employee assistance program. A myriad of voluntary benefits are available, including short- & long-term disability insurance, accident insurance, critical illness insurance, and legal assistance. We understand the importance of work-life balance and encourage employees to take advantage of our flexible work options when possible. The College offers eligible employees with a 403(b) retirement plan account and contributes 5% of their salary towards the plan. Employees receive complimentary access to our library, gym, athletic facilities, fitness center, recreational equipment, on-campus sporting events, cultural events, and social activities. Discounts are available for on-campus dining and the college’s Mercantile bookstore. We value our employees’ academic and personal interests and offer tuition remission for employees and their dependents. Employees receive complimentary access to the Paul Smith’s College Visitor Interpretive Center (the VIC), which offers 25 miles of scenic hiking, snowshoeing, and cross-country ski trails, wildlife viewing opportunities, educational programs, and interactive butterfly exhibit. For more information or questions about careers at Paul Smith’s College, please call us at: 518-327-6179 Back to Job Openings Custodian Apply Share Link copied Position: Custodian Status: Regular, Full-time, Non-Exempt Department: Campus Operations Reports to: Custodial Team Coordinator Salary: Days - $19.25/hour 1 Position Evenings - $19.25/hour 1 Position Evening differential - $1.00/hour Schedule: Days:8-hour shifts will be determined between the hours of 5:30 a.m. – 4:30 p.m. Evenings: 3 p.m.-11:30 p.m. Description: The Custodian is responsible for maintaining a clean, safe, sanitary, and welcoming campus environment for students, faculty, staff, and visitors. This position performs routine custodial duties in academic buildings, residence halls, administrative offices, athletic facilities, dining areas, and common spaces. The role supports the college’s mission by maintaining campus infrastructure and appearance in accordance with Paul Smith’s College operational, and customer service standards. Duties & Responsibilities: Clean and sanitize classrooms, offices, residence halls, restrooms, hallways, stairwells, lounges, and public areas. Sweep, mop, vacuum, dust, and polish floors and surfaces. Empty trash and recycling receptacles and transport waste to designated collection points. Clean windows, doors, walls, partitions, and furniture. Restock restroom and custodial supplies. Operate custodial equipment such as vacuums, auto scrubbers, buffers, carpet extractors, and floor machines. Assist with floor care projects including stripping, waxing, buffing, and carpet cleaning. Set up and break down tables, chairs, and equipment for campus events and meetings. Report maintenance concerns, safety hazards, and repair needs to supervisors. Follow all safety procedures regarding OSHA standards. Support emergency response activities including snow events, spills, or campus emergencies as assigned. Maintain positive customer service interactions with students, faculty, staff, and guests. Work collaboratively with team members to complete projects and goals. Perform other duties as assigned by Custodial Evening Lead or Custodial Team Coordinator or designee in their absence. Qualifications: High school diploma or GED required Previous custodial or housekeeping experience preferred but not required Ability to follow verbal and written instructions Ability to work both independently and as part of a team Basic knowledge of cleaning methods, chemicals, and equipment preferred Strong customer service orientation Ability to work with a broad range of diverse individuals and groups to form a safe and inclusive campus community. Physical Requirements: Environmental Conditions Work is consistently performed in indoor academic and residential spaces with normal temperature ranges for the season. Fast-paced environment during academic year and campus events. Traditional noise of a busy workspace setting can be expected. Working spaces may be crowded based on traffic and space configuration. Routine exposure to cleaning chemicals to perform duties. Lifting and Carrying Ability to lift up to 50 lbs. Routine lifting between 10-25 lbs. Frequent lifting and carrying light to moderate weight products or tools (cleaning tools, cleaning products, garbage, furniture items, etc.). Utilize assistive devices and equipment as necessary. Mobility Perform physically active work including bending, walking, climbing stairs, and standing for extended periods. Infrequent needs to reach overhead to perform work duties. Climbing various staircases across the campus to engage in meetings and/or presentations. Utilize mobility assistive devices and equipment as necessary. Dexterity and Hand-Eye Coordination Manual dexterity for handling cleaning tools. Sensory Requirements Good vision is required, with corrective lenses as necessary. Good hearing is required with assistive devices as necessary. Paul Smith’s College is an equal opportunity employer. Position descriptions are created that focus on essential functions, using inclusive language, and avoid unnecessary or discriminatory requirements. Applicants will be reviewed promptly and the search will move quickly, so do not delay in submitting applications. Apply Paul Smith's College Home 7777 NY-30, Paul Smiths, NY 12970 admissions@paulsmiths.edu Phone 888-873-6570 68° F Clear sky Social Facebook Instagram X YouTube TikTok Live Webcams Action Visit Apply Request Info Give Bobnet Login Footer About Paul Smith's College Faculty & Staff Directory Graduate Studies Careers Mercantile Library Directions to Paul Smith's College Privacy Policy Request Info News © 2026 Paul Smith's College . All rights reserved Site Menu Search Submit site The Smitty Story Apply for Admission First-Year Applicants Homeschooled Applicants Transfer Applicants International Applicants Graduate Applicants Cost & Aid Tuition & Fees Net Price Calculator Types of Aid Applying for Aid Payment Academics Find a Program Hands-on Learning Work Experience Program Academic Support Meet Our Faculty Graduate Studies M.S. Natural Resources Conservation M.P.S. Sustainable Tourism Management Graduate Certificates Battlefish Academy TopGuide Troops to Timber Life at Paul Smith’s College Housing & Dining Local Communities Clubs & Activities Health & Safety Alumni Athletics Search Submit Actions Visit Apply Request Info Give Bobnet Login For You Future Students Current Students Parents & Families Veterans Local Communities Alumni Center & Institutes Center for Research, Partnerships, and Innovation Adirondack Watershed Institute Institute of Adventure Hospitality & Food Institute of Forestry John Dillon Park Visitor Interpretive Center Close Close"
